I reviewed spec #5511 (the adopter lander choosing Actions or local by its median run) as a whole, fixed what the review found, and closed it.

**What happened**
- Both tickets were already closed: #5524 (the build) and #5525 (the token check on design-vault). So this was the first whole-spec review: three review axes (standards, spec, comments) over the spec's 15 commits, then a second standards pass over my own fixes. 25 findings in all.
- The one real fault: an adopter on Actions could still get no verdict in four cases, so the landing sat waiting for the next lander launch instead of testing locally. The cases were:
  - a failed run that never ran the suite, even after the lander pushed its ref again;
  - a repush that no run followed;
  - a runner that failed to start on every attempt;
  - the named-rerun daily cap being used up.

  All four now test locally on an adopter and log why. workflow-core's own lander behaves as before. The cap and runner cases went past the spec's three listed fallback cases, so I recorded that as a delegated decision on #5511.
- The tidy-up changes nothing at runtime:
  - the run record moved into its own module, `scripts/lib/lander-run-record.js`;
  - the lander jobs got their own 15-minute timeout constant;
  - one shared off-Actions builder and one log filter replace hand-written copies;
  - five renames, and the "Why:" issue lines left the generated workflow headers;
  - missing regression-test pairings were added, and leaked temp directories in the tests fixed.
- Tests: the five touched test files pass (189 tests), and typecheck is clean, re-run after the last commit.
- Landed on `main`: 715ead7bc, 94bf33457, 741a39f87 and 81f5053ef. The lander ran the full suite on ff4656472.

**What I didn't fix**
- **A missing `Weakens:` line:** commit 348a8ddab weakened an error path without one, and it has already landed, so I added the line as a comment on #5700 instead.
- **Spec findings left as they are:**
  - a cancel refusal is logged, not tested locally — a cancel carries no request to test;
  - unfinished runs stay out of the median, because they understate how long the suite takes;
  - the `ciSetup` key's release note is owed by the next version bump.
- **Expired census rows:** the close check flagged three guards (`issue-close.js`, `review-tier.js`, `anthropic-report.js`) whose measurements expired. Those files were changed by the comment sweeps and only reached this spec through merges of `main`. I filed #5713 (re-measure the 8 expired census rows) and named it on the close's `**Outstanding:**` line. #5713 is unassigned, and an agent session can do it.

The close comment on #5511 lists every finding with what happened to it, and ends `**Reviewed through:** f23b457ab4944dad36acb8367b8d68949da31b84`.

**Next:** #5713, for whichever session picks it up.

